@@ -383,6 +383,29 @@ These allow you to scope the execution time of a component.
 
 `tmax` is a read/write parameter so the user can set it to 0 to get rid of the first time initialization on the function's execution time.
 
+[[sec:hal-thread-parameters]]
+== HAL Thread Parameters
+
+(((HAL Thread Parameters)))
+Each realtime thread measures the interval between the starts of consecutive
+cycles and publishes the results as parameters named after the thread, for
+example `servo-thread.period-max`.
+All times are in nanoseconds.
+
+[horizontal]
+`.period-target` (u32, RO):: Configured period.
+`.period-last`, `.period-min`, `.period-max`, `.period-avg` (u32, RO):: Latest, shortest, longest and average measured interval.
+`.jitter`, `.jitter-avg`, `.jitter-max` (u32, RO):: Latest, average and largest absolute difference between the measured interval and the configured period.
+`.exec-avg`, `.exec-max` (u32, RO):: Average and longest time to run the thread's functions.
+`.outlier-q`, `.outlier-h` (s64, RO):: Number of intervals whose jitter was at least a quarter or a half of the period.
+`.outlier-at` (s64, RO):: Value of `samples` at the latest quarter-period outlier.
+`.missed` (s64, RO):: Number of intervals longer than two periods.
+`.samples` (s64, RO):: Number of measured intervals.
+`.stats-reset` (bit, RW):: Set to true to clear the statistics. The thread clears them, and this parameter, at the start of its next cycle.
+
+The first cycle and intervals during which threads were stopped are not measured.
+Thread names longer than 41 characters leave no room for the parameter suffixes, so such threads are created without statistics and a warning is logged.
+
 [[sec:hal-logic-components]]
 == Basic Logic Components
 
